The analysis is divided in two parts.

- Data preprocessing (Python) in "preprocessing": Datastream sample, TRTH tick data -> 5-minute liquidity
  metrics, merged panels. Outputs are Parquet files in preprocessing/data/03_output.

- Analysis in "analysis": panels (main = unbalanced, balanced = perfectly balanced), firm-level matching
  (Mahalanobis within a propensity caliper; entropy-balancing weights as robustness), figures for the
  2x2 grid {main, balanced} x {full, matched}, and the R regressions.

Both folders contain README files with the run order. CONTEXT.md is the glossary of samples, groups and
measures; docs/adr/ records the design decisions.

Run run.py to execute everything, or preprocessing/master.py and analysis/main.py by stage.

Python: conda environment in environment.yml. R: system R (>= 4.4) plus `Rscript analysis/R/requirements.R`.
